course: dictionary
lesson: 7972
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word recluse can mean a person, or a kind of spider. The words around it tell you which meaning is right, so look at the clues before you decide.
explain: A recluse is a person who lives alone and avoids being with other people. In a story, a recluse may live in a lonely house on a hill, and the children are curious about them. Often the recluse turns out to be kind.
explain: «In North America the black widow and brown recluse can give serious bites, so you do not put your hands into woodpiles or dark corners.» The clues are bites, woodpiles and dark corners, so recluse means a spider here. Check by swapping in the other meaning: a lonely person giving bites does not make sense.
fact: A recluse is a person who lives alone and avoids other people.
fact: A brown recluse is a kind of poisonous spider found in the USA.
fact: «Recluse» is a noun, so you can say a recluse or some recluses.
fact: Phrases you may meet are «live as a recluse», «a lonely recluse» and «brown recluse».
fact: Clues such as bites, woodpiles and dark corners show you which meaning is right.
exercise: «In North America the black widow and brown recluse can give serious bites.» In this sentence, what is a recluse? | *A kind of poisonous spider | A type of woodpile | A person who lives alone | A lonely house on a hill
exercise: In a story, the children are curious about the recluse in the lonely house on the hill. What is a recluse here? | A tall tree | A baker who sells bread | *A person who lives alone and avoids other people | A spider in a dark corner
exercise: «Sam wants to live as a recluse on a mountain.» What does live as a recluse mean? | Live with lots of spiders | Live in a big busy city | *Live alone and avoid other people | Live near the sea
test: «People keep their hands out of woodpiles and dark corners where brown recluses hide.» What is a brown recluse in this sentence? | A quiet neighbour | *A poisonous spider | A wooden box | A dark cupboard
test: What does a recluse avoid? | Reading books | *Being with other people | Keeping pets | Dark corners
exam: «The lonely recluse rarely left his house on the hill.» Which meaning fits best? | A poisonous spider in a woodpile | A kind of bird | A brown tree | *A person who lives alone and avoids other people
